 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs, PGAs (PGAA/PGAB gain codes are stored only), references and PDWN_REF (internal reference power-down, an input with no effect): the result is always the 0 V code (0x200 unsigned binary, 0x000 two's complement)",
  "output modes MODE/SELB (Timing Options, p.7): only the default MODE = 0, SELB = 0 (80 MHz CLK, dual-bus output, COUT = CLK / 2) is modeled; single-bus output (A and B data multiplexed on DA, DB 3-stated) is not",
  "conversions: each CLK rising edge is a conversion in the model (the device converts on alternate edges of an 80 MHz clock); pipeline latency (8/9 clocks) is not modeled",
  "COUT (pin 26) and the inverted latch clock COUT-bar (pin 25) share the name COUT in the pin table (no overbar in ASCII); the model drives both as CLK / 2, the inversion of pin 25 is not expressed",
  "OE also 3-states COUT in the device; the model's oe gates only the data pins",
  "STBY is modeled as powerdown (no conversions); the 3-state data outputs and COUT during power-down are not modeled",
  "vcc: the recommended operating table lists DVDD/DRVDD 0 (sic) to 3.6 V, 3.3 V nominal; characterization covers 3.0-3.6 V, used as the range",
  "serial interface: write-only (no read-back): the schema needs an SPI miso, so configBus names the data input as miso with protocol out/idle \"z\" (never driven); the PGA resynchronization to the internal 40 MHz clock"
